  "root_cause": {
    "manifest_half_write_rejected": "e2e_web.Stack writes sources.json once before Worker/Core startup. RecoveryStack.start_core and test_04 never rewrite it. Core loads SourceRegistry during startup; the failing request arrives after readiness.",
    "shared_object_path": "After restart, background search dispatch and HTTP web.search.start replay concurrently read the same registry contract. SourceSpec::require_review -> validate_contract -> Json::parse(input.dump()) serializes a shared json-c object.",
    "serialization_race": "json_object_to_json_string_ext mutates the object-owned print buffer. The old wrapper called it concurrently without synchronization, allowing malformed JSON to reach ShapeGuard and be wrapped as E_SOURCE_REVIEW.",
    "reference_lifetime_race": "The actual linked json-c build has non-atomic get/put reference counts, independently inspected by conditional_worker. Copies, at(), private containers holding shared children, replacement and destruction also require common synchronization.",
    "evidence_limit": "The exact CI scheduling is not replayed deterministically. Frozen synthetic shared-contract probes reproduce the same Missing colon family without any file rewrite, and independently expose a reference-count crash."
  },
